  swings         from -100° to -55°
  damping        0.04 N·m·s/rad
  starts turned  -55°

-- Upper guide walls retain ball3 on the inclined lever initially.
-- They constrain the launch vertically but remain open underneath.
-- The final lever position clears the falling-ball path.

